# Enrichment blocker report (bix-43-q1)

## What ran
- DE: Cisplatin_IC50_CBD_IC50 (9-1..9-3) vs DMSO (3-1..3-3), DESeq2-style NB GLM
  (median-of-ratios SF on all 30 samples, MoM+shrunk dispersion, Wald, BH).
- Genes tested: 15711; DE padj<0.05 & |log2FC|>1: 315 (up 174, down 141).
- Ranked gene list: sign(log2FC)*-log10(pvalue), out/ranked_gene_list.csv.

## What could NOT run and why
- gseapy prerank with GO_Biological_Process_2021: environment has NO network
  (pip install gseapy -> DNS failure; maayanlab.cloud unreachable), NO preinstalled
  gseapy/pydeseq2, NO R, and NO local GO GMT/OBO/GAF copy anywhere on disk
  (verified via filesystem-wide find for *.gmt/*.obo/*.gaf/*enrichr*/*msigdb*).
- GO_Biological_Process_2021 is an Enrichr-hosted library; without network or a
  supplied snapshot the required enrichment cannot be executed. Per agreement,
  no enrichment statistics or GO term answer were fabricated.

## Unverified directional observations from DE (NOT a substitute for GSEA)
- Up in combination: CDKN1A, BTG2, AEN, GDA, AHRR, ALDH1A3 -> p53/DNA-damage
  response and AhR/xenobiotic metabolism signatures.
- Down in combination: FOS, FOSB, EGR-family (AP-1 immediate-early), plus HIF/glycolysis
  targets (GPI, PFKFB4, ALDOC, P4HA1, KDM3A, SCD).
- If any GO BP term dominated in the original online analysis, a cell-cycle/mitosis or
  DNA-damage-response family term is the a-priori candidate from these data, but this
  is a hypothesis, not a gseapy result.

## Reproduction
Run `python3 analysis_cbd_cisplatin_de.py` (this sandbox). The enrichment step
(gseapy.prerank, ranking column=rank_metric, min_size=15, max_size=500,
permutation_num=1024, library=GO_Biological_Process_2021) requires network/gseapy.
